+Local diagnostic reports and desktop live reporting contain local data only, not remote data. Remote SSH is independent
+of the desktop network switch: disable the host to close that subscription. The app verifies a digest-addressed bundled
+collector and runs its no-argument stdio bridge. Same-UID connections share one collector daemon through a private Unix
+socket, with independent timezone views. No HTTP server, TCP listener, Python runtime or sudo is required.
+
+Optional mobile live-activity authorization is separate: after the user creates an activity in the foreground, an
+activity-scoped lease can authorize the daemon to send only minimal current metrics over verified HTTPS to
+`https://agent-speed.yooztech.com`. Confirmed authorization can survive the last SSH exit, subject to host logout policy,
+and ends at lease expiry, replacement or revocation. Closing SSH alone does not revoke it. This sends no raw logs,
+commands, conversation content or SSH credentials; the target host receives no Apple provider key. It updates existing
+activities only and does not request alerts or promise ten-second iOS rendering. See the complete
+[shared collector/control-v2 contract](docs/shared-collector.md) and [network specification](spec/NETWORK.md#8-activity-scoped-mobile-relay).
 
