+## 8. Activity-scoped mobile relay
+
+This opt-in authorization is distinct from desktop reporting and SSH subscriptions. A mobile app must create a real
+ActivityKit activity in the foreground, obtain an expiring activity lease through App Attest, and deliver it over
+host-key-verified SSH. Only requested control-v2 frames negotiate this behavior; old clients receive no unsolicited
+control frames. The exact schema, acknowledgment and timeout rules are in `docs/shared-collector.md`.
+
+Each effective-UID/executable-digest daemon may POST only to `https://agent-speed.yooztech.com/v1/publish`, using the opaque bearer
+lease. The body contains one minimal `snapshot`: registered host identity, actual sample time, live speed/counts,
+activity-timezone daily output and machine receive/transmit rates; unknown metrics remain null and title is null.
+No raw logs, history, transcript, project path, command, SSH credential or provider secret is uploaded. The host never
+receives an Apple private key, provider JWT, installation management credential or global relay password.
+
+TLS verifies the certificate and hostname. Redirects, proxy-environment forwarding and netrc credentials are disabled;
+URL aliases, arbitrary origins, query strings and alternate paths are rejected. DNS/connect is bounded to three
+seconds, the whole request to six seconds, and responses to 4096 bytes. Publishing is off the collector/SSH loop and
+keeps only the latest real sample, at least ten seconds apart; it does not replay a backlog or rewrite timestamps.
+
+A positive subscription acknowledgment requires the first successful fresh-sample publish. A confirmed lease may
+outlive every SSH subscription but cannot exceed its authorized expiry (at most eight hours); the daemon cannot
+renew it. Explicit lease unsubscribe, replacement and terminal relay rejection stop that publisher. The mobile app
+separately revokes relay authorization; activity-level DELETE operations must not race a newer lease. With no clients
+or authorized leases, the daemon exits after 30 seconds. Host logout/cgroup policy may kill it earlier; no system
+service or linger policy is installed. Only existing activities are updated: no alert, sound, banner, ordinary
+completion notification or push-to-start is sent. Local relay verification does not prove Cloudflare/APNs/iPhone delivery.
+
